WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.295 --> 00:00:02.574
Imagine trying to sell water in a beer can,

2
00:00:02.783 --> 00:00:06.765
calling it Liquid Death, and convincing people to actually buy it.

3
00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:11.969
In 2017, advertising creative Mike Cessario noticed something.

4
00:00:12.183 --> 00:00:14.773
Beer and energy drinks had exciting marketing.

5
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:15.848
Healthy drinks?

6
00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:16.899
Mostly boring.

7
00:00:17.395 --> 00:00:18.650
So he tried something different.

8
00:00:18.871 --> 00:00:21.424
What if water looked like a heavy-metal energy drink?

9
00:00:21.645 --> 00:00:23.823
What if the name was so outrageous,

10
00:00:23.943 --> 00:00:25.186
people couldn't ignore it?

11
00:00:25.431 --> 00:00:26.615
He called it Liquid Death.

12
00:00:28.381 --> 00:00:29.259
But there was a problem.

13
00:00:29.515 --> 00:00:32.972
Finding someone to put still mountain water into aluminum cans,

14
00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:34.768
at scale, wasn't easy.

15
00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:38.136
And investors weren't automatically convinced anyone wanted it.

16
00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:39.583
The product was simple.

17
00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:41.029
The packaging was not.

18
00:00:42.393 --> 00:00:45.768
Instead of waiting, they launched a provocative video before selling

19
00:00:45.888 --> 00:00:47.066
their first cans.

20
00:00:47.288 --> 00:00:48.189
Millions watched.

21
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.823
Suddenly, retailers and distributors wanted to know how to get it.

22
00:00:52.034 --> 00:00:54.451
They sold the idea before the product existed.

23
00:00:55.386 --> 00:00:57.454
Going viral doesn't guarantee profit.

24
00:00:57.628 --> 00:00:59.102
The water was canned in Austria,

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:00.568
then shipped to America.

26
00:01:00.753 --> 00:01:04.609
When COVID disrupted shipping, container costs jumped from four thousand

27
00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:06.322
to thirteen thousand dollars.

28
00:01:06.518 --> 00:01:09.059
They sold more, and lost money on every case.

29
00:01:09.891 --> 00:01:11.221
That's what many people miss.

30
00:01:11.425 --> 00:01:13.926
A brilliant brand can attract customers,

31
00:01:14.141 --> 00:01:18.755
but manufacturing, distribution and margins decide whether the business works.

32
00:01:18.959 --> 00:01:20.824
Liquid Death was selling identity.

33
00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:23.916
The biggest opportunity isn't inventing something new.

34
00:01:24.113 --> 00:01:26.595
It's making people excited about what they already buy.
